# BYD Atto 3 five-door compact SUV, 2023 onwards.
#
# The Atto 3: BYD's first UK model, with the 60.48 kWh Blade battery, the
# 150 kW front motor and the distinctive cabin with the rotating screen. UK
# order books opened on 8 March 2023 and deliveries began on 15 March.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BYD_Atto_3
#
# Dimensions 4.455 x 1.875 x 1.615 m, wheelbase 2.720 m (BYD press release
# specification table, 8 March 2023). The width over mirrors is 2.050 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a TRUE level side elevation, square to the left
# flank at about 1.2 m, so the flank is traced from it.
#
# Colours: grade (d); Parkour Red is the only UK name recorded, and the
# modelled colourways use plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 80/300, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 80. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro March 2023, the UK delivery date; retires staggered 2046-2049.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/byd-atto-3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/byd-atto-3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/byd-atto-3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the flank is traced from the square side photograph and
# reconciled to the published dimensions; the nose, partly hidden by a
# charging post, is reconstructed from the front three-quarter view. The rear
# pillar texture, lamp internals and skid trim are simplified.


obj=citycar
name=BYDAtto3(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2023
intro_month=3
retire_year=2049
retire_month=6
speed=160
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=300

